"""Manually authored claim records; no source-heading classification or automatic verdicts."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];O=R/'parts/b'
items={x['id']:x for x in json.loads((O/'items.json').read_text())};C=[]
def c(n,ii,st,status,cl,fate,refs,comp,conf='high',date='First circulation of this exact elementary identity not established; checked literature dates below.'):
    it=[items[f'SA04-{x}'] for x in ii]
    C.append(dict(id=f'C-SA04-{n}',items=[x['id'] for x in it],cote='93',scans=sorted(set(s for x in it for s in x['scans'])),lines=[y for x in it for y in x['lines']],his_statement=' | '.join(x['his_words'] for x in it if x['his_words']),statement=st,status_on_pages=status,computation=comp,class_=cl,fate=fate,fate_date=date,present_status='As of November 2026: '+({'C':'the exact unrestricted formulation remains unproved or needs the correction specified; no novelty or priority claim is made. ','F':'the statement or source attachment cannot be identified precisely from the supplied witnesses. '}.get(cl,''))+st,refs=refs,confidence=conf))

calc='programs/b_computations.py; outputs/b_computations.json; '
c(201,[202],'A natural coherent target is not forced to be omega squared without a generation or local epimorphism hypothesis: adjoining an unused direct summand O preserves the proposed invariant conditions.','false as stated','C','Searches B-Q03–04 found no theorem with these exact coherent-target quantifiers. Dumas §3.1–3.2 treats the classical omega-squared target; Hoshi Definition 1.2 fixes its target as part of the data. Neither classifies every coherent recipient. The direct-sum counterexample is proved in this audit.',['BDumas2009','BHoshi2024'],'proof_checks.md §2, direct-sum argument.','high')
c(202,[203],'Multiplication of a cocycle by a unit gives a semilinear torsor isomorphism; arbitrary multiplication, including 12, gives a pushout but need not be an isomorphism. Fibrewise nonzero scalar multipliers are units.','proof sketched','B','B-Q01/03/06 located the projective torsor in Deligne I Proposition 5.8 and its normalized cocycle in 5.9.2. The pushout statement itself follows by multiplying transition cocycles; “most refined” is not proved by this operation.',['BDeligne1970'],'proof_checks.md §2, torsor cocycles.','high','Deligne: Harvard seminar autumn 1969; publication 1970. No separate first-circulation date established for this elementary pushout statement.')
c(203,[204],'The fixed-characteristic uniqueness proposal needs a precise finite-order/naturality/category formulation; its nonvanishing condition alone is not a proof, and the manuscript margin questions it.','open on the pages','C','B-Q02–04 and backward references from Hoshi were searched. Hoshi §3 constructs a characteristic-two Schwarz system with a locally exact differential target; §6 Remark 6.4.2 records degeneration of its ordinary level-one Schwarzian for p≤3. Wakabayashi §1.7 assumes odd p. None proves the exact all-operator fixed-p uniqueness asserted here.',['BHoshi2024','BHoshi2020','BWakabayashi2021'],'No classification certificate; only small-characteristic diagnostics under C-SA04-122 and proof_checks.md §3.','medium','Hoshi first circulation April 2020, publication 2024; Wakabayashi arXiv 7 September 2021. Exact proposed classification not located by 19 November 2026.')
c(204,[205],'The third-order Schwarzian identities make sense for real C^3 local diffeomorphisms with continuous output; subsequent complex-root quotient constructions require separate sign and regularity hypotheses.','stated without proof','B','B-Q01/03 followed the classical Schwarzian references. Dumas §3.1 supplies the complex formula; the real C^3 extension of the identities follows by the same chain-rule calculation. No source found making every later analytic quotient valid unchanged in the real category.',['BDumas2009'],calc+'proof_checks.md §§1–2.','high','Dumas survey 2009; these are classical differential identities, with no first-priority date established here.')
c(205,[206],'On a smooth complex curve d:O to omega is a sheaf epimorphism with locally constant kernel; dg-df is its translation cocycle, with initial-value uniqueness and canonically trivial additive quotient.','proof sketched','E','B-Q08 and Deligne I §2.4, Theorem 2.17 were checked for the local analytic connection setting. Local integration gives the exact rank-one assertions, re-proved here. The fate is elementary classical analysis, not a later research theorem.',['BDeligne1970'],'proof_checks.md §1; no numerical certificate needed.')
c(206,[207],'The Pro E_X to omega epimorphism is false with fixed f, while the Codex O_X reading is true. Replacing it by local coordinates to omega-star and dg/df gives the valid construction.','corrected by himself later','E','B-Q08 and the local analysis in B-Q01 verify the local integration framework; the decisive target -df counterexample and corrected unit-valued integration are independent here. The authorial correction is scan76:1045–1053, conditional on the Pro reading of scan75:1033–1034.',['BDeligne1970'],'proof_checks.md §1.','high')
c(207,[208],'For a holomorphic line bundle on a smooth complex curve, frames modulo locally constant scalars are locally the same as connections; dlog:O-star/C-star to omega is a sheaf isomorphism.','stated without proof','E','B-Q08; Deligne I Definition 2.4 and Theorem 2.17 give the connection/local-system framework. The rank-one quotient is re-proved by primitive and exponential. It is local, with no global horizontal-frame conclusion.',['BDeligne1970'],'proof_checks.md §1.')
c(208,[209],'With horizontal-frame convention, D_g-D_f=-dlog(g/f); the affine-coordinate quotient is Conn(omega). Positive signs printed for the connection difference have the opposite convention.','false as stated','E','B-Q08; Deligne I §2.3.5 fixes the usual Leibniz rule. The sign follows directly from it and is independently checked; the exact manuscript convention is not decided by a literature match.',['BDeligne1970'],calc+'horizontal_frame_sign_f_t_g_t2; proof_checks.md §1.')
c(209,[210],'The inverse-differential invariant g/dg is scale invariant, has initial-value rigidity away from zero, and is not onto all vector fields. Restriction to nonzero coordinates yields locally solvable dlog equations.','corrected by himself later','E','B-Q08; local ODE theory in Deligne I §2 supplies the setting. The author explicitly rejects the old range on scan77:1118–1127. Counterexamples and the corrected solution formula are independent proofs here.',['BDeligne1970'],'proof_checks.md §1.')
c(210,[211],'The correct logarithmic ratio is (dg/df)(f/g). Its square is the inversion-invariant quotient; the earlier product with g/f is false.','false as stated','E','B-Q01/08 found the classical quotient framework; the exact correction is an algebraic identity, checked against the later internal formulas on scans82 and84 rather than inferred from a broad reference.',['BDumas2009'],calc+'log_ratio_correct and wrong_ratio_test_f_t_g_t2; proof_checks.md §2.')
c(211,[212],'Homogeneity of the value space is proposed as a condition for successful quotient constructions, without a precise general theorem.','open on the pages','F','B-Q03/04 searched universal/coherent invariants and Hoshi’s Schwarz-system formulation. Those theories do not identify the unspecified success criterion. No necessity or sufficiency theorem can be matched to this heuristic.',['BHoshi2024'],'Textual comparison only; no mathematical assertion with fixed quantifiers to prove.','low')
c(212,[213],'Over C, the scaling-and-inversion quotient of nonzero local coordinates is the frame torsor of omega squared via (dlog f)^2; equality means f=cg or c/g locally.','proof sketched','E','B-Q01/03/08; the classical projective framework is documented by Dumas §3.1. The exact elementary subgroup quotient is re-proved by square roots and integration here; no positive-characteristic identification is claimed.',['BDumas2009'],'proof_checks.md §§1–2.')
c(213,[214],'For nonzero n over C, taking a root of a framed n-differential and a primitive gives a well-defined projective coefficient c_n=-2f-double-prime/(nf)+(2n+1)(f-prime/f)^2/n^2, with horizontal beta_n=-dlog(f)/n.','proof sketched','B','B-Q03 searched n-differential/projective connections; B-Q06 followed Deligne I §5.9–5.12. The exact coefficient follows from the classical connection-to-projective construction and is re-derived here. Neither the word “nonzero” nor invertibility of n can be removed.',['BDeligne1970','BDumas2009'],calc+'cn_from_horizontal_connection; proof_checks.md §2.','high','Classical projective construction documented in 1969 seminar/1970 publication; no independent first-circulation date for this c_n notation located.')
c(214,[215],'The mixed coefficient c_n(g)-c_m(f) must use f-prime/f in the f term; the transcribed g-prime/g there is false.','false as stated','B','B-Q03/06 found the underlying classical formula. This exact typographic or authorial error is resolved algebraically, not historically, by substitution in c_n.',['BDeligne1970'],calc+'wrong_second_term_test; proof_checks.md §2.')
c(215,[214],'Mixed c_n differences satisfy the cocycle identity and c_nr(f^r)=c_n(f) for nonzero n,r; the subscript 0 used for a coordinate-input map is not substitution n=0.','proof sketched','B','B-Q03/06; Deligne I §5.9.1 is the classical cocycle setting. The exact mixed-weight and power formulas are independently proved by cancellation and substitution, retaining n,r invertible.',['BDeligne1970'],calc+'tensor_power_cn and proof_checks.md §2.')
c(216,[216],'The cancelled and repeated factor12 rescaling does not specify an unambiguous canonical torsor normalization; a difference takes values in the acting sheaf, and reversing arguments reverses sign.','open on the pages','F','B-Q01/06 matched Deligne I §5.9.2, where theta=S/6 and the manuscript G=-12theta. This fixes a comparison of conventions but cannot identify which cancelled torsor label was intended on scan80.',['BDeligne1970'],'proof_checks.md §2 for the algebra; textual comparison for the renamed torsor.','medium')
c(217,[217],'Fractional linear substitutions with coefficients from the base leave the relative integral invariant unchanged.','stated without proof','B','B-Q01–04; Deligne I §5.9.3 proves projective-coordinate invariance in characteristic zero. The all-base Hasse identity is separately checked under C-SA04-122; a characteristic-zero citation alone is not its proof.',['BDeligne1970'],'Cross-reference C-SA04-122; proof_checks.md §3 uses the verified integral three-jet identity.','high')
c(218,[217],'In characteristic zero equality df=dg forces projective equivalence locally. This ordinary-differential criterion fails for integral G_0 in characteristics2 and3.','stated without proof','B','B-Q01–04; Dumas §3.1 gives zero-Schwarzian/projective equivalence in characteristic zero. Hoshi §6 confirms that small characteristic needs another comparison; the explicit Hasse counterexamples are proved here.',['BDumas2009','BHoshi2024'],calc+'proof_checks.md §§2–3.','high')
c(219,[218],'Proportional logarithmic derivatives with arbitrary constant c do not imply vanishing projective invariant; f=t squared, g=t, c=2 gives nonzero 3(dt/t)^2.','open on the pages','B','B-Q01/03/06; the classical vanishing criterion requires a projective transformation, not an arbitrary power. The counterexample decides the strongest natural reading of the manuscript question.',['BDumas2009'],calc+'arbitrary_power_test_G_t_t2; proof_checks.md §2.')
c(220,[219,220],'The unfinished terminal expression and the questioned cover/path diagram do not determine complete maps with identifiable source, target, and descent conditions.','open on the pages','F','B-Q06/08 compared Deligne I §1.3 and Proposition1.7 (local systems and path action). These results require specified action data and do not identify D,U,B,V,Sigma or the disputed cancellation scope.',['BDeligne1970'],'Textual comparison of Pro80–81 and Codex09:166–247 only; no proof claim.','low')
c(221,[220],'A relation (c lambda,xi) equivalent to (c,lambda xi) is an associated-bundle quotient if a right action on c and compatible left action on xi are specified.','stated without proof','C','B-Q06/08; Deligne I §1 provides the path-action framework. The usual quotient construction is established, but the draft does not supply the actions needed to instantiate it.',['BDeligne1970'],'Conditional formal quotient check; no proof of the unspecified draft construction.','medium')
c(222,[221],'Conditionally on E=Omega inverse direct-sum O, its twisted trace-zero endomorphisms are Omega direct-sum O direct-sum Omega squared; on a compact smooth connected genus g≥2 complex curve their section count is4g-2.','proof sketched','C','B-Q03 and Stacks Lemma53.5.2(tag0B5B) supply Riemann–Roch/duality. The genus count is a conditional inference; the uncertain E and cancellation cannot be identified from that theorem.',['BStacks0B5B'],'proof_checks.md §7; outputs/b_computations.json genus_count.','medium')
c(223,[222],'Nonvanishing h is insufficient for an etale solution of f+1/f=h; the derivative degenerates at f=±1 and h=2 is a counterexample.','open on the pages','E','B-Q08 local analytic ODE/inverse constructions were searched; elementary quadratic calculation settles this exact question. It is not an open problem in current theory.',['BDeligne1970'],calc+'reciprocal_map; proof_checks.md §2.')
c(224,[223,224,225],'Power ratios are multiplicative and the nonzero frame power map is a local epimorphism over C for n nonzero. A formula using -1/n requires n nonzero; the attachment of the Pro zero-index label remains uncertain. Missing frame stars would change the defined range.','stated without proof','E','B-Q03/08; the elementary local-root calculation supplies the result. The nearby -1/n dlog supports Codex n≠0, but mathematics does not decide the ink.',['BDumas2009'],'proof_checks.md §2; textual comparison of the two witnesses for n and stars.')
c(225,[226],'The affine-to-projective map has coefficient2lambda-prime+lambda squared and variation2D eta+eta squared; applying it to the derivative frame recovers G.','proof sketched','B','B-Q01/03/06; Deligne I §5.12 compares second-order differential equations and projective connections. The exact normalization here is checked independently rather than equated without a scalar.',['BDeligne1970'],calc+'gamma_variation and gamma_beta1_d; proof_checks.md §2.','high','Documented classical comparison: Deligne seminar1969, publication1970.')
c(226,[227],'Exponentiation intertwines sign/translation with scaling/inversion, and dlog(exp f)=df induces the identity differential arrow.','proof sketched','E','B-Q01/08 checked the local analytic context; the identity is elementary and was independently recomputed. No global logarithm is assumed.',['BDumas2009'],calc+'exponential_correction; proof_checks.md §2.')
c(227,[228,226],'The quadratic-input map is delta(fdt²)=c_t+[f-f-double-prime/f+(5/4)(f-prime/f)^2]dt², and delta(alpha²)=gamma beta_1(alpha)+alpha².','false as stated','B','B-Q03/06 found the classical projective coefficient construction. Substitution fixes the formula under the displayed definition, while Pro/Codex disagree about the actual linear term and coefficient reading.',['BDeligne1970'],calc+'delta_squared; proof_checks.md §2.')
c(228,[238],'Projective line bundles and degree-two Azumaya algebras correspond etale-locally; a global P(E) presentation exists only when its Brauer obstruction vanishes. Line-twist and rank-two duality identities hold for actual E.','stated without proof','A','B-Q07 opened Grothendieck Brauer I §5.1–5.3 and §8.1–8.4: these give precisely the etale-local algebra/projective description and the obstruction to a global vector-bundle presentation. Stacks59.62.1 gives line-twist ambiguity. ClassA records his own published formulation; the undated leaves are not thereby proven earlier.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI','BStacks0A2J'],'proof_checks.md §4, real conic counterexample and tensor identities.','high','Bourbaki talk May1965; collected seminar publication1966. Chronology of the undated manuscript relative to that talk is not established.')
c(229,[239],'For rank two, trace kernel equals Gamma²E tensor det(E)^-1 and scalar quotient equals Sym²E tensor det(E)^-1; they cannot be conflated at2.','stated without proof','B','B-Q07 searched divided/symmetric squares and trace-zero matrices, without finding an exact source for this displayed pair of sequences. The characteristic-free tensor statement is independently proved by its canonical basis map; no priority or later-discovery claim is made. Grothendieck Brauer I §7.5 supplies the commutator-algebra setting.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI'],'proof_checks.md §4; explicit symmetric/alternating tensor bases.','high')
c(230,[240],'For quotient P(E), T_relative=O(2) tensor det(E)^-1 and its pushforward is End(E)/O.','stated without proof','A','B-Q07; Grothendieck Brauer I §8.5 identifies the infinitesimal projective action, and Stacks§27.21(tag01OA) fixes the quotient convention. The determinant twist follows from the universal quotient sequence, proved here.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI','BStacks01OA'],'proof_checks.md §4.','high','Grothendieck Brauer I: talkMay1965/publication1966; no date assigned to this manuscript leaf.')
c(231,[241],'The pgl2 and sl2 bracket tables have factors1 and2 as displayed; the pgl2 Killing determinant is-32, so its nondegeneracy requires2 invertible.','proof sketched','E','B-Q02/04/07/09 searched SGA3 and sl2 automorphisms. The classical bracket tables are independently recomputed, with their exceptional prime made explicit. No exact first date for the normalization is asserted.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI'],calc+'pgl2_brackets,Killing_matrix,Killing_det,sl2_brackets; proof_checks.md §4.')
c(232,[242],'The questioned canonical equivariant identification M=f_*P1_relative(T) fails at2: the latter splits as O plus g, while M has no conjugation-invariant scalar retraction there. It works via trace/2 after inverting2.','open on the pages','C','B-Q03/07/08 searched principal parts/projective connections and the matrix-algebra comparison. Stacks10.133.6 supplies the jet exact sequence, but no exact published answer to this specific canonical identification was located. The stated equivariant obstruction is an independent proof, not a novelty claim.',['BStacks09CN'],'proof_checks.md §4; jet_rank output is only the rank diagnostic.','high')
c(233,[243],'The center of End(E) is O and its quotient is the infinitesimal projective vector-field algebra. This does not identify every Lie automorphism with a projective automorphism.','stated without proof','A','B-Q07; Grothendieck Brauer I §7.3–7.5 and §8.5 establish the algebra/group/infinitesimal projective setting. The central quotient is checked in a matrix basis; the stronger Lie-automorphism assertion is treated separately.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI'],'proof_checks.md §4.','high','TalkMay1965/publication1966; no relative manuscript date inferred.')
c(234,[243],'The trace-zero map sl2 to pgl2 is an isomorphism when2 is invertible, and fails at2 because the scalar center lies in sl2.','stated without proof','E','B-Q04/07/09; the exact map is elementary linear algebra. Its failure is independent of the valid fppf central quotient of the groups.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI'],calc+'sl2_brackets; proof_checks.md §4.')
c(235,[244],'Over a field of characteristic not2, the adjoint map PGL2 to AutLie(sl2) is an isomorphism; in characteristic2, AutLie(pgl2)=GL2 semidirect G_a², so the unqualified identification fails.','open on the pages','B','B-Q09 located Alberca et al., arXiv1508.01634, §7, pp.15–16, Corollary4 and Lemma13, for the exact non-2 field automorphism result. The characteristic2 pgl2 calculation here is independent and must not be replaced by a statement about sl2 or o3.',['BAlberca2015'],'proof_checks.md §4; outputs/b_computations.json char2_automorphisms.','high','Alberca et al. arXivfirstposting7August2015; original first date of the elementary non-2 theorem not established here.')
c(236,[245],'Projective points correspond to the appropriate rank-two direct-summand left ideals, described as endomorphisms killing the kernel line. Two transverse points give complementary ideals as modules.','proof sketched','A','B-Q07; Grothendieck Brauer I §8.1–8.4 gives the projective/Azumaya correspondence. The exact left-ideal description and its module-only direct sum are checked by matrices here.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI','BStacks01OA'],'proof_checks.md §§4–5.','high','Own published correspondence May1965/1966; matrix description has no first-priority date assigned.')
c(237,[246],'The standard rank-two GL2 representation does not descend through PGL2, since scalars act nontrivially.','stated without proof','E','B-Q07; the central quotient and Brauer obstruction in Grothendieck Brauer I explain the relevant setting. The representation obstruction is checked directly, without claiming that PGL2 lacks all faithful representations.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI'],'proof_checks.md §4 and scalar action on E.')
c(238,[247],'A marked projective section produces a rigidified relative O(1) and an extension0→Omega→L→O→0, compatible with local trivializations.','proof sketched','B','B-Q07/08; the projectivization convention in Stacks01OA and the marked P1 description in Beilinson–Drinfeld §2.7 match the construction’s setting. The explicit divisor-sequence proof is supplied here; no unmarked global splitting is assumed.',['BStacks01OA','BBDOpers2005'],'proof_checks.md §5.')
c(239,[247],'Restriction of the rigidified O(1) to the first neighbourhood of the section identifies its rank-two pushforward; this requires I², not I.','proof sketched','B','B-Q08; Stacks10.133.6(tag09CN) distinguishes first jets from restriction to the section. The exact projective calculation follows from O(-1) having no H0 or H1, proved locally here. The exponent on the scan remains unsettled.',['BStacks09CN'],'proof_checks.md §5; jet_rank output.')
c(240,[247],'The complement of the marked section is an Omega-torsor; a second disjoint section splits it, and reversing the ordered pair dualizes the conormal line.','proof sketched','B','B-Q07/08; projective quotient and marked-section frameworks match in Stacks01OA and BD§2.7. The torsor is explicitly the retractions of the marked extension, giving the exact claim independently.',['BStacks01OA','BBDOpers2005'],'proof_checks.md §5.')
c(241,[249],'The adjoint bundle of the marked extension has filtration with graded lines Omega,O,Omega inverse and middle extension L; recovery is possible with the marking, although Pro/Codex disagree about the direction asked.','proof sketched','B','B-Q08; BD§1.1–1.2 and §3.3 provide the filtered adjoint/Borel framework. The displayed transition matrix independently checks this exact rank-two case. No direction of the uncertain manuscript sentence is selected.',['BBDOpers2005'],calc+'upper_triangular_transition; proof_checks.md §5.')
c(242,[250],'The quotient g/Omega is L-dual via Killing only when2 is invertible; a nonsplit extension of O by O on a characteristic2 elliptic curve gives a counterexample otherwise.','open on the pages','B','B-Q04/07/08/09 searched the characteristic restriction. BD§3.2 uses a nondegenerate invariant pairing in characteristic zero; it does not supply a characteristic2 extension. The exact nonsplit-extension counterexample is independently proved here.',['BBDOpers2005'],calc+'upper_triangular_transition; proof_checks.md §5.')
c(243,[251],'SL2/mu2=PGL2 as fppf sheaves in every characteristic; at2 this is not an etale central kernel.','stated without proof','A','B-Q02/07 searched SGA3 and Grothendieck Brauer I. The central-quotient construction occurs in BrauerI§1.4 and the scheme forms in§7.1–7.3; the fppf determinant-square-root proof here checks the topology at2.',['BGrothendieckBrauerI'],'proof_checks.md §5.','high','Grothendieck talkMay1965/publication1966. SGA3seminar1962–1964/publication1970 metadata checked; no unopened SGA theorem is credited.')
c(244,[247,245],'Two ordered disjoint sections split L as Omega plus O, and yield complementary annihilator ideals; this is a module decomposition, not an algebra product.','proof sketched','E','B-Q07/08; projective quotient conventions in Stacks01OA support the construction. Direct matrix-column decomposition gives the precise statement here.',['BStacks01OA'],'proof_checks.md §5.')
c(245,[254],'A local constant bracket basis gives a local flat reference connection; a global reference connection is not supplied by that choice.','stated without proof','E','B-Q08 and Deligne I §2.4–2.9 were checked. This is the local trivial-connection construction and cannot resolve global torsor obstruction.',['BDeligne1970'],'proof_checks.md §6; direct trivialization check.')
c(246,[255],'Every derivation of the three-dimensional algebra is inner when2 is invertible; the unqualified assertion is false at2 and explicitly restricted by the author on scan90.','corrected by himself later','B','B-Q04/09; Alberca et al. §7, p.15, before Lemma12, computes all sl2 derivations over a ring with2 invertible. The manuscript’s characteristic2 failure is exhibited by D(e)=f,D(h)=D(f)=0, not inferred from a broad citation.',['BAlberca2015'],calc+'char2_outer_derivation; proof_checks.md §4.','high','Alberca arXiv7August2015 records the classical field result; no first-discovery date is claimed. Manuscript correction:89:2052–2057 to90:2160–2163.')
c(247,[256,255],'The inner-connection adjoint matrix gives the two successive graded maps with c12=-2c23. Bracket-preserving connections alone do not force this at2 because outer derivations exist.','proof sketched','B','B-Q08/09; BD§1.2 supplies oper transversality, and Alberca §7, p.15, supplies the 2-invertible innerness calculation. All displayed matrix entries and the characteristic2 obstruction are independently checked.',['BBDOpers2005','BAlberca2015'],calc+'connection_ad_matrix and transverse_factor; proof_checks.md §6.')
c(248,[256],'For a projective connection, the normal coefficient vanishes exactly when the marked section/Borel filtration is preserved; the graded second fundamental forms are O-linear.','proof sketched','B','B-Q08; BD§1.2 and §2.7 identify the marked-section transversality setting. O-linearity and the zero criterion follow directly from Leibniz and the adjoint matrix.',['BBDOpers2005'],'proof_checks.md §6.')
c(249,[257],'Connections form a locally nonempty g tensor omega torsor; the normal-component quotient has a canonical zero in Borel frames, and a fixed normal component leaves an L tensor omega torsor.','proof sketched','B','B-Q08; Deligne I §2.6 supplies the difference-of-connections principle; BD§1.2 and §3.2 specialize it to the adjoint filtration. The precise Borel gauge argument is given independently. Global nonemptiness is not automatic.',['BDeligne1970','BBDOpers2005'],'proof_checks.md §6.')
c(250,[258],'The restriction C_Omega has first-order symbol the inclusion and quotient -2i; in characteristic2 it may lose data retained by the quotient restriction. Fixing i and C_Omega leaves an Omega tensor omega difference.','proof sketched','B','B-Q08; Stacks10.133.6(tag09CN) supplies the universal first-jet framework, while the factor2 and lost information follow from the exact manuscript matrix. No characteristic2 equivalence is imported from the complex oper literature.',['BStacks09CN'],calc+'transverse_factor; proof_checks.md §6.')
c(251,[258],'If -2i is an isomorphism, then2 is invertible, omega is a line bundle, and the restricted data are uniquely L=P1(omega) tensor omega inverse with its universal first-order operator. Conversely that restricted construction exists under these hypotheses.','proof sketched','B','B-Q08; Stacks10.133.6 gives the principal-parts exact sequence and universal operator. BD§3.3 describes the canonical Borel object over a smooth complex curve. The exact two-extension argument here proves the stated restricted-data result, without a full global connection assertion.',['BStacks09CN','BBDOpers2005'],'proof_checks.md §6.')
c(252,[258],'Full compatible transverse connections still form an omega-squared torsor; over a smooth complex curve their marked P1 description is precisely a PGL2-oper/projective connection.','stated without proof','B','B-Q01/08; BD§2.7 gives the marked P1 description and§3.1–3.3 the quadratic-differential torsor and canonical Borel object. Deligne I Proposition5.8 is a direct classical predecessor. No general arithmetic or Gauss–Manin conclusion follows.',['BBDOpers2005','BDeligne1970'],'proof_checks.md §6; independent remaining-a matrix calculation.','high','Deligne seminar1969/publication1970; BD text written1993, arXiv23January2005. These document development, not priority of the undated manuscript.')

# C244 duplicated the splitting/ideal clauses of C240 and C236; consolidate them.
C=[x for x in C if x['id']!='C-SA04-244']
for x in C:x['class']=x.pop('class_')
assert len(C)==51 and len({x['id'] for x in C})==51
(O/'claims.json').write_text(json.dumps(C,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({'claims':len(C),'ids':[C[0]['id'],C[-1]['id']]}))
